From 8828e75a7f662ab064b875d7916dcfebe568cb02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Brill <opensource@christophbrill.de>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:36:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] GP-0: Add x86-16 Pascal calling conventions

Parameters pushed left-to-right could not be expressed in a
prototype, so Win16 Pascal functions got reversed parameter order.

Add the "stackltr" attribute on <input>. Stack parameters are
assigned as usual, then mirrored so the first parameter sits at the
highest address. The decompiler also reverses recovered stack
trials. Add __pascal16near and __pascal16far to x86-16.cspec.

ATTRIB_UNKNOWN moves from id 161 to 162 in Java and C++.

Closes #496
