 the hidden return will come first.
 </para>
 <para>
+The <emphasis>stackltr</emphasis> attribute indicates that parameters passed on the stack are pushed
+left-to-right, as in the Pascal calling convention. The first parameter then sits at the highest
+address, and the last parameter is closest to the return address. Parameters passed in
+registers are not affected. This attribute is not supported when the stack grows positively.
+</para>
+<para>
 The following is an example tag using the standard allocation strategy with 3 integer registers and 2
 floating-point registers. If there are more parameters of either type, the compiler allocates storage from
 the stack.
